croeconomic effects of an increase in indirect tax on animal products (Figure 2 and Extract A, line 17). Use a relevant diagram to support your answer.","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["indirect tax","tax incidence","animal products","meat"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":27,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p2-2025-jun-q4a","p":43,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(a)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"In 2023 the UK government reduced indirect tax on certain goods and services. Define the term ‘indirect tax’.","topics":["2-6-2-demand-side-policies","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-2"],"keywords":["indirect tax","definition"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p2-2025-jun-q4c","p":43,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(c)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"In 2023 the UK government reduced indirect tax on certain goods and services. Which one of the following is an example of an indirect tax?","topics":["2-6-2-demand-side-policies","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-2"],"keywords":["indirect tax","VAT","taxation"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed","type":"mcq","options":["Corporation tax","Income tax","Inheritance tax","Value added tax"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2025-jun-q2a","p":24,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(a)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain the cost of a subsidy on the market for cooking oil to the Indian government (Extract E, line 6).","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["subsidy","cost of a subsidy","demand and supply diagram","India"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":33,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q6f","p":33,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(f)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q6-choice","marks":20,"questionText":"Evaluate the likely impact of a tax on plastic food-packaging. Use a diagram to support your answer.","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["indirect tax","plastic packaging","tax incidence","diagram"],"qpPage":14,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":12,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q4b","p":7,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Patrick Street Productions produces musicals. Its latest production is ‘It’s a Wonderful Life’ and the total cost of this production is $200 000. The ticket price is $40. The theatre has a capacity of 300 seats. The company aims for revenue maximisation. If this is achieved, revenue from ticket sales will cover 30% of total costs. Charitable donations contribute 12.5% towards total cost and a government subsidy ensures the production covers all of its costs. Calculate the value of the government subsidy necessary for this production to cover all of its costs.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-3"],"keywords":["subsidy","total costs","calculation","theatre"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed"},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q6d","p":7,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(d)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"With reference to Extract C, discuss the proposed government subsidy to prevent Thomas Cook from reaching its shut-down point.","topics":["3-3-4-normal-profits-supernormal-profits-losses","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-3"],"keywords":["shut-down point","subsidy","losses","Thomas Cook"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id"